      "description": "Watch Tottenham vs Charlton Athletic highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 26, 2026. The Carabao Cup spotlight fell on North London on August 26, 2026, as Tottenham Hotspur welcomed Charlton Athletic for a high-stakes knockout encounter. Fans gathered in anticipation of a classic cup tie, with the hosts looking to assert their dominance against their spirited lower-league opponents. Early Disruptions and Defensive Resilience The match began with an unexpected series of events for Charlton Athletic , who suffered a double injury blow within the first 15 minutes. Collins Sichenje and Billy Koumetio were both forced off the field, necessitating the early introductions of Dan McNamara and Lloyd Jones . Despite these tactical setbacks, Charlton remained compact and difficult to break down. Tottenham dominated possession, but their early efforts were met with stubborn resistance, and Lucas Bergvall even picked up a yellow card in the 24th minute as the hosts grew frustrated by the deadlock. A Late First-Half Surge The pressure finally told in the closing stages of the first half. In the 41st minute, Mikey Moore ignited the stadium with a brilliant left-footed finish into the top center of the goal, assisted by Rodrigo Bentancur . The momentum shifted entirely in favor of the Spurs, and they struck again just four minutes later. Dominic Solanke found the bottom corner from the center of the box after a well-placed pass from Moore following a corner. This quick-fire double sent Tottenham into the break with a commanding two-goal lead. Commanding the Second Period Tottenham continued their offensive onslaught after the restart. After a series of saves by Charlton’s Tiernan Brooks , the hosts added a third in the 67th minute when Kevin Danso rose highest to head home a cross from Mateus Fernandes . The introduction of Sávio off the bench provided even more spark; he scored a sensational long-range goal in the 82nd minute before turning provider for Ben Davies just three minutes later. The scoreline reflected a clinical performance by the Premier League side, who left little room for error. Charlton’s Consolation and Injury Concerns To their credit, Charlton Athletic refused to give up and managed to pull one back in the 87th minute. Lloyd Jones powered a header into the center of the goal following a cross from Joe Rankin-Costello , giving the traveling fans something to cheer about. The match ended 5-1, but there was a late shadow cast over the victory as Micky van de Ven required treatment for an injury in stoppage time. Nevertheless, Tottenham Hotspur comfortably secured their place in the next round with an emphatic display."
